WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.050
What's wrong?

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.750
You've been in a daze for awhile.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.550
It's nothing.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.500
Maybe you're not awake yet.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.500
Who was he?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.950
Yuya, are you good at trivia?

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.940
Trivia?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.650
Okay!  Let's go the next question!

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.050
Question!

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.650
Sherlock Holmes was an expert 
on what musical instrument?

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.920
Solving mysteries!

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.250
Kyuando, you were the fastest!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.600
Violin!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.890
Correct!

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.100
Huh?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.800
Wrong again, Yuya!

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.800
But he's a detective, right?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.050
Isn't he good at solving mysteries?

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.150
He said "musical instrument."

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.000
You're so careless.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.040
Be quiet!

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.500
Next question!

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.950
Earth's dia-

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.310
Kyuando!

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.350
12,742 kilometers!

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.450
Correct!

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.220
The question was “What 
is Earth's diameter?”

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.900
The winner is Eita Kyuando!

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:22.050
Wow!  He answered the question 
the moment it was read aloud!

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.350
He's big news right now!

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:32.040
He's won all the quiz shows, so he's 
known as the “Universe of Knowledge.”

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.300
He's totally different than someone we know.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.510
Don't look at me when you say that!

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.650
Kyuando, what does trivia mean to you?

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.250
It's my life!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.750
Knowledge is the culmination 
of everyday effort.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.100
It lets me learn what is 
correct and incorrect in life.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.690
That's what I believe!

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:57.150
But since Yuya always 
gives the wrong answers...

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.630
Stop pitying me!

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.840
I have no interest in trivia!

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.940
Though I said that, I watched 
quiz shows until the morning.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.600
Most of my answers were wrong.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:20.120
Even if I'm not good at trivia, that 
doesn't affect my entertainment dueling!

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.700
We'll see about that.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:35.200
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:40.080
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.580
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.380
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.160
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.570
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.310
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:22.880
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.080
Impulse  Got it got it

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.290
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.050
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:47.970
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.910
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.310
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:05.590
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.930
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.970
Universe of Knowledge!!  Eita Kyuando

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.380
Let's enter.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.770
Yeah.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:35.350
Isn't Clarity School a 
super-famous prep school?

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.500
Yes.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.480
This school nurtures students into top-class

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.460
politicians, scholars and 
leaders in a variety of fields.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.430
This school trains people into 
becoming winners at life!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:54.000
They also train duelists, of course.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.900
Knowledge is...

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.550
Number one!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.900
The correct answer is...

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.690
Only one!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.590
You're...

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.550
He's my school's top student.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.350
The King of Quizzes!

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.450
The Universe of Knowledge Eita Kyuando!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.200
You seem to know who I am.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.270
What an honor.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:30.700
I saw Pendulum Summon on video.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:31.740
Nice to meet you.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:35.950
Yeah.  I saw you on a quiz show yesterday.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.950
Let's have fun today!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:38.750
Thank you in advan-

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.450
Time for a question!

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.620
Question?

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.850
You were about to say "Thank you in advance."

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:50.350
How do you say that in French?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.050
French?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:55.370
The time limit is ten seconds.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.850
Ten seconds?

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:03.310
Umm...  Thank-a you-a in-a advance-a?

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.250
Incorrect!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.900
The answer is "merci d'avance."

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.950
Merci?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.650
Incorrect.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.750
You are incorrect, Sakaki.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.650
You don't even know how to say it in French.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.100
And you dare say “Thank 
you in advance” to me?

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:35.850
C'mon!  Who cares if I don't know merci!

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.100
My apologies.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:42.100
Everyone has things they're good 
at and things they're bad at.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.980
I'm good at riddles!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.450
That is promising.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:51.190
What are you bad at, other than French?

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.400
Why do I have to tell you?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.660
If you tell me yours, I'll tell you mine.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.130
I'm bad at science and math.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.750
Science and math...

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.100
Well?  What are you bad at?

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.700
Bad?  Me?

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.100
I'm not bad at anything!

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.500
Nothing?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:20.100
I'm good at some things, 
but I'm bad at nothing!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:25.050
Because I'm perfect!

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.830
Stop lying!  Everyone is bad at something!

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.400
It's the truth.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:34.550
When it comes to knowledge, 
Kyuando has no weaknesses.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.810
Exactly, Mr. Bad-at-Math-and-Science.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.680
Go!

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.500
Attack him directly!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.200
I lose.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.820
Incredible.  He won in an instant.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:01.250
Was this checkmate?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.950
It was fun, but it wasn't satisfying.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:09.050
I need - no, I will - become stronger!

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.900
Yuya's duel should've started by now.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.370
Do your best.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.050
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.950
The duel will now begin!

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.800
First up is Clarity School's ace!

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:26.800
Since he keeps studying, he truly 
is the “Universe of Knowledge!”

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:32.300
The gifted quiz whiz Eita Kyuando!

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.900
Knowledge is...

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.030
Number one!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:44.700
Facing him is the heir to entertainment 
dueling and the pioneer of Pendulum!

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:48.670
Yuya Sakaki!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.900
Yuya!

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.550
Action Field on!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.650
I activate the Field Spell Quiz Quest!

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.520
Knowledge is light!

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.250
Knowledge is love!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.950
Knowledge is the weapon that 
opens humanity's success!

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:14.200
Clarity School proudly represents 
the frontier of success!

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.650
It's Quiz Quest!

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.050
Quiz Quest?

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.080
Exactly!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.550
I'm an expert on this field 
because it requires knowledge.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:31.450
I'm the most dazzling and 
strongest on this field!

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:40.350
I wonder how Yuya's entertainment 
duel will work in a quiz field.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:44.730
The duelists meet at the battlefield!

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.870
Along with their monsters,

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:50.570
they'll kick the ground and fly through 
the sky to move around the field!

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.100
Witness!

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:54.640
Dueling's greatest evolution!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.450
Action!

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.300
Duel!

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.550
Time for a question!

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:15.150
Who will go first in this duel?

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:17.230
Kyuando!

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.450
Correct!

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.000
My turn!

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.300
I summon Quiz Monkey from my hand!

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.150
A monster with 0 attack points?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:35.450
0 is both the beginning 
and end of everything.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:39.200
0 has infinite potential!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:44.050
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.260
Yuya, he's bluffing!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:54.650
I'm looking forward to your 
specialty - Pendulum Summon.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:57.000
If you can pull it off.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.500
My turn!

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.640
I draw!

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.100
I summon Performapal Bowhopper!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:09.880
All right!  It's a monster 
with 1500 attack points!

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.500
Here I go!  Battle, Bowhopper!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.900
Attack Quiz Monkey!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:22.900
Quiz Monkey's effect activates!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:30.060
When it battles, you must 
guess how many Quiz Monsters

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:35.500
will be left on the field at 
the end of the Battle Phase!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:42.550
If you answer correctly, 
you gain 1000 life points!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:48.720
If you're incorrect, I can Special Summon 
this card if it's in the graveyard.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.200
Then one of your monsters is destroyed,

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.260
and my monster's attack and defense points 
become the same as your destroyed monster.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:59.150
What's your answer?

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:03.200
Umm...  Uhh...  Come again?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.350
One last time!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:12.300
At the end of battle, how many 
Quiz Monsters will be on my field?

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.680
Your Quiz Monkey has 0 attack points.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:20.300
Bowhopper has 1500 attack 
points, so it can't lose!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.100
The answer is zero!

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.900
Sakaki's answer is zero!

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.250
What's the correct answer?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.200
All right!  I'm correct!

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:41.400
After I pretend that you're correct, I 
activate the Continuous Trap Not So Fast!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:50.740
Once per turn, my Quiz Monster isn't 
destroyed in battle, and I take 0 battle damage!

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:53.480
The battle is over!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.310
What's this?

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:58.620
Sakaki's answer was zero monsters!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:00.760
However...

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:04.340
There's one Quiz Monkey on my field!

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.970
Too bad!  You're incorrect!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:11.870
Therefore, Bowhopper is destroyed!

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:20.190
Quiz Monkey's attack points 
become the same as Bowhopper's!

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:25.820
Aww!  If Yuya answered "one," 
he would've been correct!

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.570
No, the result wouldn't change.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.290
If Yuya answered "one,"

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:35.480
Eita wouldn't activate his trap and 
would let his monster be destroyed.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:39.650
No matter what I answered, 
I would've been wrong!

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.450
Whoa!  You're correct for once!

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:46.910
I determine what's correct and incorrect.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:50.810
I have the initiative?  Correct!

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:54.220
You have the advantage?  Incorrect!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.770
I end my turn.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.000
It's time for a question!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:09.370
Who's the pathetic duelist who will take 
damage from a direct attack next turn?

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:14.680
Well?  It's such an easy question!

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:19.650
The answer is you, Yuya Sakaki!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.640
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.880
That's right.  You have 
to rely on Action Cards.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:33.120
Let's battle!

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:36.970
Quiz Monkey attacks you directly!

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:40.860
I got it!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.450
Action Trap activates.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:50.870
Welcome!  Quiz action!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.990
Action Trap?

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:56.110
This Action Card will 
allow you to avoid damage.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.080
All right!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.710
But only if you answer the quiz correctly.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.280
What?  Quiz?

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:08.220
If you're incorrect, you can't avoid the 
damage, and you also lose 100 life points.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.540
What?

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:14.320
All Action Cards on this 
field are determined by

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.500
whether you answer the quiz 
correctly or incorrectly.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.980
Everything is a quiz.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.020
I'm dazzling!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.910
Is this for real?

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:26.510
Let's begin.

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.910
The genre is Science for 100.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.910
Science?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:34.000
There's a cup full of water.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.480
Ice is floating inside.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:42.400
When the ice melts, will 
the water overflow or not?

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.120
Which is it?

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.400
It will overflow!

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.220
Incorrect.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:51.200
I await your next attempt.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.040
And Quiz Monkey attacks you directly!

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:09.710
It's refreshing to witness 
such a wonderful mistake!

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:18.160
When a Quiz Monster deals you battle damage,

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.960
I can Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.250
I Special Summon Quiz Sphinx from my hand!

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:32.740
When there's a Quiz Monster on my 
field, you can't attack this card!

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.050
Let's battle!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:37.710
Quiz Sphinx attacks you directly!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.000
How wonderful!

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.570
You're bad at both quizzes and dueling!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.020
Damn...

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:55.330
I humbly end my turn.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.170
My turn!

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:05.650
As long as he has Quiz Monkey and Not 
So Fast's effects, what can I do?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.280
I'll deal with them by using an Action Card.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.310
I drew science last time, which I'm bad at.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.450
I just need to draw a card in another genre!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:18.450
Keep running.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.020
But I'll make the first move.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:27.130
You'll be totally disgraced.

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:30.570
I made it here before you!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.930
Action Trap activates.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:38.900
Welcome!  Quiz action!

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:42.820
If you're correct, you gain 300 life points.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:46.150
The genre is Trivia for 300.

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:47.800
Question!

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:51.050
What's inside a raccoon's treasure chest?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.000
Nothing!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.750
Correct!  You gain 300 life points.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.730
If you remove “ta” from “treasure chest,” you get “nothing!”
(Note: This is Japanese wordplay.)

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.700
I know that!

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.900
I'm going to the next one!

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:06.370
I got it!

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:09.000
Action Trap activates.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.750
If you're correct, you gain 500 life points.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:16.200
The genre is Trivia for 500.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:20.580
Question: In what kind of 
competition does the loser laugh?

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.300
A staring contest!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:26.100
Correct!  You gain 500 life points.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:30.020
I also knew that answer!

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.260
I'll keep going!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.660
Action Trap activates.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.140
It's getting repetitive.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.200
Understood.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:47.100
If you're correct, you gain 1000 life points.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:50.200
The genre is Trivia for 1000.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:54.600
Question: Which gets more sun 
- the road or the sidewalk?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.450
Sidewalk!

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:56.600
Correct!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:01.700
Because “road” in English is “shadow.”
(Note: This is Japanese wordplay.)

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:05.000
I didn't know that one.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.200
5800 life points.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.200
This is bad.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.670
Damn!  In that case...

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.900
I have to get that Action Card!

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:29.000
Action Trap activates.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.250
If you're correct, you gain 100 life points.

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.350
If you're incorrect, it will be the opposite.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.770
Bring it on!

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.260
The genre is Math for 100.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.330
Math?

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.650
Question!

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:46.240
If you place pillars 10 meters apart,

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.540
how many pillars do you need for 100 meters?

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.600
I know this!

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.510
It's 100 divided by 10, so the answer is 10!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.350
What?

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.650
The correct answer is 11.

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:09.160
You would've known if you thought about it.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.190
Next one!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.090
There it is!

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:19.050
Question!

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:21.550
The genre is Math for 200.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.900
There are two dice.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:27.400
The first die rolled a 6.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:31.210
What are the odds that the 
second die will also roll a 6?

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.950
Umm...  Two 6's, so the odds are 12!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:43.960
Sheesh, he didn't even 
understand the question.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.750
Question!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:50.160
The genre is Science for 300.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:55.630
300kg of steel and 300kg of 
cotton - which is heavier?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.200
Cotton!

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.900
You won't trick me!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.800
Yuya...

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:07.200
Listen carefully to the question.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.820
Even I knew the answer.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.200
How sad that you're only drawing 
genres that you're bad at.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.760
I'm good at trivia, but he drew them all.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:22.600
He made sure to get rid of the 
genre that I could answer.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:27.500
That means all that's left 
are the ones I'm bad at.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.030
Damn!

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:32.050
It's time for a question.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:35.470
Who's the pitiful duelist 
who's about to struggle

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:42.400
against truly hellish quizzes 
and disgrace himself?

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:44.080
Truly hellish?

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.600
I activate an Action Card!

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:56.000
The heaven of knowledge will 
guide the stupid to hell!

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:59.850
Quiz Quest - Extra Stage!

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:06.600
The answer is you, Yuya Sakaki!

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:18.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:28.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:45.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:01.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:06.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:17.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:23.100
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:32.440
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:40.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:50.090
Card illustration question: How 
many teeth does Pot of Greed have?

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:52.550
What?  There's no way I remember!

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:54.580
The answer is 20 teeth.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:58.950
Next question: How many people 
are flying in Heavy Storm?

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.420
That's easy!  Two people!

00:24:01.420 --> 00:24:02.650
Incorrect!

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:09.450
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Difficult Questions!?  Attack Duel Quiz!!

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:11.430
What's the answer to the quiz?

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.900
You'll have to watch the next episode!
